// Reading integers out of a byte buffer.
//
// Every module here reads a file it did not write, so the bytes arrive as an
// `int[]` -- one byte per cell, bounds-checked on every read. A wrong offset
// aborts rather than returning a number from somewhere else in the document,
// which is the whole reason not to put them in the flat store.
//
// Little endian is how ZIP and DEFLATE write; big endian is how TrueType
// does. See ../../../NAMES.md.
//
// There is no `rd_u8`. It would be `xs[at]`, which is `idstd`'s `lget`, and
// two functions with one body are a compile error -- correctly: a byte is
// read by indexing, and a name for that is a name for nothing.

rd_le16(int[] xs, int at) {
} return int xs[at] + xs[at + 1] * 256;

// A `word`, because a full 32-bit field does not fit an `int`: a CRC or a
// size with the high bit set would come back negative, and the caller would
// have no way to tell that from a small file.
rd_le32(int[] xs, int at) {
  word a = rd_le16(xs, at + 2);
} return word rd_le16(xs, at) + a * 65536;
